error[E1703]: an import path starts with `./`, `../` or `@`
 --> imports.dat:4:20
4 | import { PI } from "math";
  |                    ^^^^^^ file paths start with `./` or `../`, and the standard library with `@dat/`
fix: import `@dat/math` from the standard library
4 | import { PI } from "@dat/math";

error[E1401]: floor is not defined
  --> imports.dat:11:9
11 |   print(floor(area(2.0)), sqrt(16.0));
   |         ^^^^^ `floor` comes from `@dat/math`
fix: import `floor`, `sqrt` from `@dat/math`
 4 | import { PI, floor, sqrt } from "math";

error[E1401]: sqrt is not defined
  --> imports.dat:11:27
11 |   print(floor(area(2.0)), sqrt(16.0));
   |                           ^^^^ `sqrt` comes from `@dat/math`; the fix on line 11 imports it
